WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.244
The very next day, Tommy went to Dr. Dolittle’s house.

2
00:00:05.245 --> 00:00:08.225
Of course, the doctor wasn’t home.

3
00:00:08.226 --> 00:00:12.270
But Tommy got to meet a very friendly dog.

4
00:00:12.271 --> 00:00:16.977
For a week, Tommy went to Dr. Dolittle’s house every day.

5
00:00:16.978 --> 00:00:22.563
Every time he visited, though, he found that the doctor still had not returned.

6
00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:26.081
"When is he coming back?" Tommy asked the dog.

7
00:00:26.082 --> 00:00:30.006
The dog let out two short barks.

8
00:00:30.007 --> 00:00:33.284
"I wish I could understand animal language, too,"

9
00:00:33.285 --> 00:00:37.192
sighed Tommy before he went home.

10
00:00:37.193 --> 00:00:39.663
The friendly dog’s name was Jip.

11
00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:42.675
He liked Tommy the first time he saw him.

12
00:00:42.676 --> 00:00:45.418
He especially liked the treats he brought.

13
00:00:45.419 --> 00:00:48.758
That’s why he didn’t growl or bark at him.

14
00:00:48.759 --> 00:00:55.497
"Jip, you’re supposed to be guarding the house!" Dab-Dab the duck scolded him one day.

15
00:00:55.498 --> 00:00:59.800
"I’m just taking a break," Jip replied sleepily.

16
00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:03.156
Dab-Dab swatted Jip with his broom.

17
00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:06.279
"Did that boy come again?" he asked.

18
00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.845
"Ouch!" Jip jumped up. "Yes, he did!"

19
00:01:10.846 --> 00:01:12.782
"I wonder what he wants?"

20
00:01:12.783 --> 00:01:17.045
Dab-Dab said as he swept the steps.

21
00:01:17.046 --> 00:01:20.713
Gub-Gub the pig came out munching on a cake.

22
00:01:20.714 --> 00:01:25.624
"You’re dropping crumbs all over the steps!" Dab-Dab shouted.

23
00:01:25.625 --> 00:01:31.997
Gub-Gub tried to pick up his mess, but succeeded only in stepping on Jip’s tail.

24
00:01:31.998 --> 00:01:36.965
"Oh!" Jip yelped and chased after the pig.

25
00:01:36.966 --> 00:01:42.838
"Jip! Gub-Gub! Stop it!" Dab-Dab shouted after them.

26
00:01:42.839 --> 00:01:46.576
Meanwhile, Tommy was getting worried about the squirrel.

27
00:01:46.577 --> 00:01:51.065
"It doesn’t look good," he told Jip the next time he visited.

28
00:01:51.066 --> 00:01:54.127
"I hope the doctor comes home soon."

29
00:01:54.128 --> 00:01:59.644
Jip barked. Just then Tommy heard a low rumbling sound.

30
00:01:59.645 --> 00:02:03.082
He looked up at the sky.

31
00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:05.270
"It looks like a big storm.

32
00:02:05.271 --> 00:02:07.884
I’d better get home," he said.

33
00:02:07.885 --> 00:02:12.365
Suddenly Jip sniffed the air and began barking excitedly.

34
00:02:12.366 --> 00:02:15.301
"What is it, boy?" Tommy looked around.

35
00:02:15.302 --> 00:02:19.141
But he could not see anything.

36
00:02:19.142 --> 00:02:21.411
Tommy ran down the path.

37
00:02:21.412 --> 00:02:25.918
Just as he turned onto the road, a heavy rain started to fall.

38
00:02:25.919 --> 00:02:29.618
He covered his head and ran as fast as he could.

39
00:02:29.619 --> 00:02:35.034
He didn’t see the man walking toward him.

40
00:02:35.035 --> 00:02:41.318
"Oooh! Aw! Ouch!" they exclaimed as they crashed into each other.

41
00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:43.407
"I’m terribly sorry, sir!"

42
00:02:43.408 --> 00:02:47.511
Tommy shouted over the sounds of the storm.

43
00:02:47.512 --> 00:02:51.558
"I’m the one who should be sorry," the man said, chuckling.

44
00:02:51.559 --> 00:02:53.368
Tommy was amazed.

45
00:02:53.369 --> 00:02:57.858
No adult had ever been so kind to him before.

46
00:02:57.859 --> 00:03:00.870
"Do you live far from here?" the man yelled.

47
00:03:00.871 --> 00:03:03.508
"Yes, sir," Tommy answered.

48
00:03:03.509 --> 00:03:06.574
"Then come to my house and wait till the storm stops."

49
00:03:06.575 --> 00:03:08.726
The man began walking.

50
00:03:08.727 --> 00:03:10.416
Tommy followed him.

51
00:03:10.417 --> 00:03:16.512
But in the heavy wind and rain, it was hard to see where they were going.

52
00:03:16.513 --> 00:03:22.004
They arrived at a gate and walked up to the man’s house.

53
00:03:22.005 --> 00:03:25.094
"What a storm!" the man said.

54
00:03:25.095 --> 00:03:28.448
He had very kind eyes and a kind smile.

55
00:03:28.449 --> 00:03:32.460
Tommy liked him immediately.

56
00:03:32.461 --> 00:03:35.428
"That’s odd. Where is everyone?"

57
00:03:35.429 --> 00:03:38.446
the man said after he opened the door.

58
00:03:38.447 --> 00:03:43.436
Suddenly the room was filled with bright lights and loud barnyard noises.

59
00:03:43.437 --> 00:03:45.891
Tommy hid behind the man.

60
00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:49.620
"Oh, how delightful! Oh, wonderful!"

61
00:03:49.621 --> 00:03:53.359
the man said and clapped excitedly.

62
00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.745
Tommy could not believe his eyes.

63
00:03:55.746 --> 00:03:58.623
Surrounding him were all kinds of animals.

64
00:03:58.624 --> 00:04:04.803
They snorted, quacked, barked, hooted, squeaked, and chirped happily at the man.

65
00:04:04.804 --> 00:04:09.474
But more amazingly, the man answered them back.

66
00:04:09.475 --> 00:04:12.647
Tommy recognized the dog he saw every day.

67
00:04:12.648 --> 00:04:17.078
Suddenly he realized they were at the famous doctor’s house!

68
00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:21.857
Meanwhile, the man was talking to the dog in strange barking sounds.

69
00:04:21.858 --> 00:04:24.358
What he was really saying was:

70
00:04:24.359 --> 00:04:26.705
"Do you know this boy, Jip?"

71
00:04:26.706 --> 00:04:31.713
"Yes, doctor! He came every day to wait for you," Jip replied.

72
00:04:31.714 --> 00:04:35.156
"How do you do?" the man shook Tommy’s hand.

73
00:04:35.157 --> 00:04:37.252
"I’m Dr. Dolittle."

74
00:04:37.253 --> 00:04:41.488
Tommy was speechless.

